What does Media Transfer Operator do at WPP Production?
&nbsp;
The Media Transfer Operator is responsible for the quality control of broadcast assets across ingest and delivery. Central to this is the QC of both incoming video &amp; audio assets to be used by our editors and VFX teams, and the QC of finished TV commercials before delivery to play-out partners and Broadcasters.  &nbsp;&nbsp;

Responsibilities:

• The role of the Media Transfer Operator is to ensure work being delivered for either client approval or broadcast is delivered to specific requirements and is timely.

• The ideal candidate will have a proven background in broadcast QC and delivery, and a strong working knowledge of standard video codecs &amp; formats, encoding, standards conversions and file delivery. Experience in uploading/downloading assets from/to DAM sites or Cloud Portals is preferred. A working knowledge of Adobe Premiere and After Effects is also required.&nbsp;

• Ingest QC / Output QC &amp; delivery encodes of TV commercials for broadcast&nbsp;

• Monitor Scope, Waveform &amp; Audio Meters to ensure required specifications.&nbsp;

• QC of Premiere &amp; After Effects projects to determine completeness and suitability for adaptation&nbsp;

• Encoding/Transcoding files using Adobe Media Encoder to international delivery&nbsp;&nbsp;

• Resolution, Aspect Ratio and Standards Conversions using optimum settings.&nbsp;

• Overall responsibility for the technical quality of files and the appropriateness of the standards, created for distribution&nbsp;

Requirements:

• Strong experience in an MCR capacity in a post-production facility and/or agency

• Strong knowledge of broadcast QC and international delivery specifications&nbsp;

• Excellent understanding of compression codecs, formats and deliverables&nbsp;

• Basic I/O management in Adobe software, especially Premiere Pro and After Effects.

• Able to adapt to new working methods, technology advances and able to switch between multiple methods for multiple clients.&nbsp;

• Strong and Consistent attention to detail is highly essential

• Excellent time management skills and multitasking abilities

• Positive attitude towards problem solving and tight deadlines

