Anduril Industries is a defense technology company with a mission to transform U.S. and allied military capabilities with advanced technology. By bringing the expertise, technology, and business model of the 21st century’s most innovative companies to the defense industry, Anduril is changing how military systems are designed, built and sold. Anduril’s family of systems is powered by Lattice OS, an AI-powered operating system that turns thousands of data streams into a realtime, 3D command and control center. As the world enters an era of strategic competition, Anduril is committed to bringing cutting-edge autonomy, AI, computer vision, sensor fusion, and networking technology to the military in months, not years.

ABOUT THE TEAM &nbsp;

&nbsp; The Lethality team is a diverse, multidisciplinary group with one common goal: to enable Anduril products to achieve decisive effects on target. The team brings over 100 years of combined experience designing, analyzing, manufacturing, testing, and fielding ordnance assemblies designed for complex operational environments. &nbsp;
&nbsp;
Our engineers and technicians work closely with multiple business lines to provide core warhead and explosives&nbsp;expertise&nbsp;for Anduril. This vertically integrated approach allows us to design and develop payload solutions directly alongside the delivery vehicle, enabling Anduril to&nbsp;provide&nbsp;the warfighter operational capabilities faster than ever before. &nbsp;
&nbsp;
The Lethality team&nbsp;operates&nbsp;with a strong bias toward execution and a hands-on commitment to delivering on schedule. Team members are expected to take ownership, work directly with vehicle teams, collaborate across engineering and operations, and rapidly turn technical concepts into reliable, safe, and performant systems that can be produced and deployed at scale &nbsp;

ABOUT THE JOB &nbsp;
&nbsp;
Our warfighters need lethal systems capable of deterring our adversaries and defending our allies. The Anduril&nbsp; Lethality Team &nbsp;is looking for a&nbsp; Senior/Staff Mechanical Engineer &nbsp;who is up for the challenge: lead new warhead designs from prototype to production at Anduril speed. This role is focused on warhead mechanical design, platform integration, modeling and simulation, performance testing, qualification assessment, and transition to production. &nbsp;

Yes, you heard that right! We want to pay you to blow stuff up! &nbsp;

This role is a strong fit for creative engineers who are willing to learn and want to take ownership in leading a program developing new mechanical designs from the ground up. We are a hands-on, fast-paced team working on technically demanding systems where mechanical design and system safety have a direct impact on mission outcomes. &nbsp;

At the Senior level, a background in warhead design is strongly preferred but not&nbsp;required. Strong mechanical concept development skills, hands-on experience leading teams to develop complex systems, and a continued desire to learn are the keys to being successful in this role. &nbsp;

WHAT YOU'LL DO &nbsp;

• Lead warhead and complex ordnance/munitions system designs from prototype to production. &nbsp;

• Develop mechanical designs, drawings, specifications, test procedures, technical reports, and engineering documentation. &nbsp;

• Create high-fidelity prototype assemblies and assess performance through rigorous testing. &nbsp;

• Execute and manage arena, ground, flight, and system-level testing of munitions products, including high-speed video capture, data analysis, and design iteration based on results. &nbsp;

• Develop project plans, program schedules, design-of-experiments, and coordinate safety protocols. &nbsp;

• Work with vendors, suppliers, and subcontractors supporting critical design, prototype, test, and production efforts. &nbsp;

• Support the assembly and disassembly of explosive test articles and precision targets. &nbsp;

• Operate in a fast-paced environment

